WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.042 --> 00:00:05.380
♪

00:00:16.307 --> 00:00:18.309
(narrator)
It's called the beautiful game

00:00:18.309 --> 00:00:19.102
for a reason.

00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:20.937
A distinction
accurately painted

00:00:20.979 --> 00:00:23.314
by the game's legendary
artist-- Pelé.

00:00:23.314 --> 00:00:25.191
Football, or soccer
as it's known in the US,

00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:27.944
is the number one sport
in 93 countries.

00:00:27.986 --> 00:00:30.989
Most important
is to do, for the--

00:00:30.989 --> 00:00:33.033
the foreigners,

00:00:33.074 --> 00:00:36.161
for the people who gonna
be there, nice show,

00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:39.497
and the-- and they receive
it well, the people there.

00:00:39.497 --> 00:00:41.833
(narrator)
And one can link
its worldwide popularity

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:43.376
to its simplicity.

00:00:43.418 --> 00:00:44.961
No financial obstacles,

00:00:45.003 --> 00:00:47.172
because all you need
is a football.

00:00:47.172 --> 00:00:48.631
I think it's the only game
in the world

00:00:48.673 --> 00:00:50.550
that brings every
single country together.

00:00:50.592 --> 00:00:52.844
Yes, it's one language,
it's football,

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:56.514
but what sport does is,
it brings everyone together.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.141
It gets everyone talking.

00:00:58.183 --> 00:00:59.684
(narrator)
From back alleys
and side streets,

00:00:59.684 --> 00:01:01.686
to muddy fields
and scorched sand,

00:01:01.686 --> 00:01:05.065
it can be played anywhere
by anyone,

00:01:05.106 --> 00:01:06.900
boys and girls,
rich and poor.

00:01:06.941 --> 00:01:09.027
It's inviting
to all walks of life.

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:13.323
Football now is a sport
which is taken very seriously.

00:01:13.364 --> 00:01:16.534
(narrator)
For 3,000 years,
this has been the world's game.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:20.205
And for many centuries,
every legend started
from the same point.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.373
From Beckham to Pelé
and Sir Bobby Charlton,

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:26.211
their journey began the same
manner as everyone else.

00:01:26.211 --> 00:01:27.712
For 3,000 years,

00:01:27.712 --> 00:01:29.255
this has been
the world's game.

00:01:29.297 --> 00:01:30.882
And for many centuries,

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:33.218
every legend started
from the same point.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:36.888
Cristiano Ronaldo, star player
for Real Madrid and Portugal,

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.599
was molded from the same
humble beginnings.

00:01:53.321 --> 00:01:54.531
♪

00:01:54.572 --> 00:01:57.325
(thunder cracking)

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:59.119
(camera shutter clicking)

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.579
(narrator)
On the fifth of February, 1985,

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.081
a baby boy was born

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:05.750
to Maria Dolores
dos Santos Aveiro,

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:09.087
and José Dinis Aveiro.

00:02:09.087 --> 00:02:12.006
They were simple people,
making their way through life

00:02:12.048 --> 00:02:15.260
as a cook and a gardener
in Santo Antonio, Funchal.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:17.137
This small town is located

00:02:17.178 --> 00:02:18.763
on the island
of Madeira, Portugal,

00:02:18.763 --> 00:02:21.099
overlooking the ocean.

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:23.768
Santo Antonio
means Saint Anthony,

00:02:23.768 --> 00:02:26.771
and on that day, a saint
was indeed delivered

00:02:26.771 --> 00:02:28.940
into the world of football.

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:32.277
Cristiano Ronaldo
dos Santos Aveiro.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.946
Named after his father's
favorite actor,

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:38.116
US President Ronald Reagan,

00:02:38.116 --> 00:02:41.953
Ronaldo's early life hardly
resembled a Hollywood movie.

00:02:41.953 --> 00:02:44.622
His rag to riches story
begins with a childhood

00:02:44.622 --> 00:02:46.791
rooted in severe poverty.

00:02:46.791 --> 00:02:49.460
His Catholic family,
like many others in the town,

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:52.046
struggled to survive.

00:02:52.088 --> 00:02:54.299
Food and shelter
were considered luxuries.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.675
And at Christmastime,

00:02:55.717 --> 00:02:58.303
there was rarely any sign
of Santa Claus.

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.138
Their house
was a tin-roofed shack

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.514
which would often leak

00:03:01.556 --> 00:03:03.641
due to the warm
and powerful thunderstorms

00:03:03.641 --> 00:03:06.519
that graced the Portugal
coast each summer.

00:03:06.561 --> 00:03:09.522
A lot of guys do
come out from,

00:03:09.564 --> 00:03:12.400
from poverty,
hard upbringings,

00:03:12.442 --> 00:03:15.278
and that's their motivation.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.822
A lot of that is the motivation
that keeps them pushing.

00:03:17.822 --> 00:03:21.159
(narrator)
Cristiano was
the youngest child.

00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:22.785
Having an elder brother Hugo

00:03:22.827 --> 00:03:26.706
and two elder sisters,
Elma and Liliana Catia.

00:03:26.748 --> 00:03:28.333
Quarters were tight,

00:03:28.333 --> 00:03:32.337
as Ronaldo, his brother,
and two sisters shared one room.

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:34.839
The dirt floor
was their bed.

00:03:34.839 --> 00:03:37.717
Crumpled clothing
served as a pillow.

00:03:37.759 --> 00:03:41.179
In addition to the financial
hardships of this family,

00:03:41.179 --> 00:03:44.807
he also found it hard
to make friends his own age.

00:03:44.849 --> 00:03:46.059
He was a lonely boy,

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.853
and his only
companion

00:03:48.853 --> 00:03:52.523
became a tattered football
he found in an alleyway.

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:55.360
He would take the ball
to a nearby wall,

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.195
and there, between
the cement and stone,

00:03:57.195 --> 00:03:58.863
he practiced.

00:03:58.863 --> 00:04:01.741
He'd spend every waking hour
with his friend,

00:04:01.783 --> 00:04:05.495
skipping meals,
and sometimes school.

00:04:05.536 --> 00:04:09.040
(man)
What inspired you
to take up soccer?

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:11.209
What inspired you
to start playing?

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:14.587
Well, that one is a tough
question, good question.

00:04:14.629 --> 00:04:16.422
(audience laughing)

00:04:16.464 --> 00:04:19.384
Hmm... I don't know
why I had football.

00:04:19.384 --> 00:04:21.552
Maybe because
the sports that I,

00:04:21.552 --> 00:04:23.471
since when I was a kid,

00:04:23.513 --> 00:04:27.725
it's what, um...
made me motivation.

00:04:27.725 --> 00:04:30.270
Maybe because
of my brother,

00:04:30.311 --> 00:04:34.232
my father, my cousins.

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:36.901
Because they all
play football.

00:04:53.251 --> 00:04:54.836
(narrator)
Ronaldo's childhood mirrored

00:04:54.877 --> 00:04:56.587
that of another
football great,

00:04:56.587 --> 00:05:00.133
Edison Arantes
do Nascimento.

00:05:00.174 --> 00:05:02.927
You probably know him
simply as Pelé.

00:05:02.927 --> 00:05:05.430
Before becoming a three-time
champion at the World Cup,

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:08.099
and scoring over 1,300 goals,

00:05:08.099 --> 00:05:10.393
Pelé's career started
with an old sock

00:05:10.435 --> 00:05:12.312
stuffed with rags.

00:05:12.353 --> 00:05:15.273
His father, a minor league
footballer, taught Pelé.

00:05:15.315 --> 00:05:17.900
And with his unmatched
dedication, he flourished.

00:05:17.942 --> 00:05:20.570
Pelé would become the youngest
player ever to win the World Cup

00:05:20.611 --> 00:05:25.283
at just 17 years old,
scoring six goals for Brazil.

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:26.659
Love!

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:28.161
(crowd)
Love!

00:05:28.202 --> 00:05:29.287
Love!

00:05:29.287 --> 00:05:30.705
Love!

00:05:30.747 --> 00:05:32.832
(narrator)
And for Ronaldo,
much like Pelé,

00:05:32.874 --> 00:05:36.419
if it wasn't about football,
it was a nuisance.

00:05:36.461 --> 00:05:38.963
Football was his life.

00:05:38.963 --> 00:05:41.299
He molded his skills
playing against everyone

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:42.967
and anyone,
young and old.

00:05:42.967 --> 00:05:45.053
Without application,

00:05:45.094 --> 00:05:48.181
your talent
doesn't mean anything.

00:05:48.222 --> 00:05:49.766
You've got to have the two.

00:05:49.807 --> 00:05:51.768
Application
without talent

00:05:51.809 --> 00:05:55.063
is difficult, but you can
still maybe get by.

00:05:55.104 --> 00:05:57.190
Um, talent without
no application,

00:05:57.231 --> 00:05:59.108
you've got no chance.

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:00.777
(narrator)
At the age of eight,

00:06:00.818 --> 00:06:03.780
Ronaldo joined amateur
local team Andorinha.

00:06:03.821 --> 00:06:06.157
At that age,
this young child was a far cry

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:08.826
from the muscled athlete
that commands the pitch today.

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:10.453
And even though
he was skinnier

00:06:10.495 --> 00:06:11.996
and less developed
than his competition,

00:06:11.996 --> 00:06:15.124
Ronaldo's talents
were recognized immediately.

00:06:15.166 --> 00:06:17.835
Ronaldo, he started off
at a really young age.

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:21.339
I mean, you know, like we all
do when we're starting football.

00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:25.134
And then when you get to sort of
an age of 10, 11, 12 years old,

00:06:25.176 --> 00:06:27.345
you'll then start finding
that these clubs will be,

00:06:27.345 --> 00:06:29.847
and professional clubs,
will be looking at you

00:06:29.847 --> 00:06:32.183
to see whether they can
actually move you forward.

00:06:32.225 --> 00:06:34.435
(narrator)
Ronaldo's skills

00:06:34.477 --> 00:06:36.104
were creating
a great deal of buzz.

00:06:36.145 --> 00:06:38.523
Smaller football clubs in Spain,
Portugal, and England

00:06:38.523 --> 00:06:41.025
are always on the lookout
for their next star,

00:06:41.025 --> 00:06:42.735
and the competition
is tough.

00:06:42.777 --> 00:06:44.570
Having the ability to
occasionally strike the ball

00:06:44.612 --> 00:06:48.574
into the goal is not enough
to get you noticed.

00:06:48.616 --> 00:06:49.909
The first thing
we look for in any player

00:06:49.951 --> 00:06:52.245
is what natural ability
he's got.

00:06:52.286 --> 00:06:53.996
Now, it's not
what we can coach him,

00:06:54.038 --> 00:06:56.040
it's what has he got
that he shows us?

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:57.542
What does he bring to us?

00:06:57.542 --> 00:06:58.876
And then after that,
you know,

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:00.628
does he got
a love for the game,

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:02.922
does he love training,
does he love coaching?

00:07:02.964 --> 00:07:04.924
Has he got a passion
for the game?

00:07:04.966 --> 00:07:06.717
And is he full
of enthusiasm?

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:09.262
But first and foremost
is his own natural ability.

00:07:09.303 --> 00:07:10.263
(narrator)
However, this was not a problem

00:07:10.304 --> 00:07:11.681
for the young Ronaldo.

00:07:11.722 --> 00:07:14.892
At just 12 years of age,
he moved 600 miles

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:18.271
from his poor small town
to the city of Lisbon

00:07:18.312 --> 00:07:20.565
where he had
an offer from Sporting.

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:23.901
He had the opportunity then
to move to a sizeable,

00:07:23.901 --> 00:07:26.821
very big club in Portugal,

00:07:26.863 --> 00:07:30.950
which then allowed him
with his family

00:07:30.992 --> 00:07:33.369
to progress
and push him forward.

00:07:33.411 --> 00:07:36.831
That's where you need
the support to actually
move forward with your career.

00:07:36.873 --> 00:07:38.916
(narrator)
Though he continued
to turn heads,

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:41.252
the transition
was not easy for Cristiano.

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:42.962
It's hard now
to imagine this player

00:07:43.004 --> 00:07:45.256
ever had a problem
with popularity.

00:07:45.298 --> 00:07:48.092
But way before the fancy cars,
expensive clothes,

00:07:48.092 --> 00:07:52.722
and supermodel girlfriends,
Ronaldo was alone.

00:07:52.763 --> 00:07:55.099
Miles from home,
in a strange city,

00:07:55.099 --> 00:07:56.601
school was a struggle,

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:58.436
and his only redemption
came on the pitch.

00:07:58.436 --> 00:08:01.772
Constantly bullied by classmates
for his Madeirine accent,

00:08:01.772 --> 00:08:03.524
and forced to be alone,

00:08:03.566 --> 00:08:06.611
he lost faith in his education
and teachers.

00:08:06.652 --> 00:08:08.446
It reached
a boiling point at 14

00:08:08.446 --> 00:08:11.949
when Ronaldo threw a chair
at an instructor.

00:08:11.949 --> 00:08:13.534
He was expelled.

00:08:13.576 --> 00:08:16.621
This was not an issue
in his mother's eyes.

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:18.289
As his biggest ally,

00:08:18.331 --> 00:08:21.334
Ronaldo's mother rallied
around her youngest son.

00:08:21.375 --> 00:08:25.004
She supported his aspiring
football career with gusto.

00:08:25.046 --> 00:08:27.465
And with his family's
backing,

00:08:27.507 --> 00:08:29.383
Ronaldo continued
his meteoric rise

00:08:29.425 --> 00:08:33.804
into the upper echelons
of the beautiful game.

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:36.599
That's what it's all about,
it's dedication, keep working.

00:08:36.641 --> 00:08:38.392
You haven't got to be
too old or too young,

00:08:38.434 --> 00:08:40.019
just keep working
at your physique.

00:08:40.061 --> 00:08:42.647
We've constantly got to
be trying to bring players

00:08:42.647 --> 00:08:44.524
into the first team squad,

00:08:44.565 --> 00:08:46.442
so the pressure's there
every year

00:08:46.484 --> 00:08:47.818
to sort of make sure
that the quality's good enough.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.362
(narrator)
But the next year,

00:08:49.403 --> 00:08:53.324
Ronaldo was dealt
another difficult card.

00:08:53.366 --> 00:08:55.034
He was diagnosed

00:08:55.076 --> 00:08:57.119
with a racing-heart
condition,

00:08:57.161 --> 00:09:01.165
(man)
Surgical ablation which
is relatively new

00:09:01.165 --> 00:09:03.167
from a minimally invasive
standpoint

00:09:03.167 --> 00:09:07.255
involves also making burn
lesions on the outside
of the heart

00:09:07.296 --> 00:09:10.299
and also getting rid
of that left atrial appendage,

00:09:10.341 --> 00:09:13.719
which is the little portion
of the heart where
the clot forms

00:09:13.761 --> 00:09:16.055
that then often can fire off
to the body.

00:09:16.097 --> 00:09:18.516
(narrator)
Thankfully for us,
his mother opted

00:09:18.516 --> 00:09:19.850
to let Ronaldo
have the operation,

00:09:19.892 --> 00:09:23.020
and the rest, as they say,
is history.

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:24.689
♪

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:26.732
Better than new,
the stars aligned

00:09:26.774 --> 00:09:31.112
for the young phenomenon
on August 12, 2003.

00:09:31.153 --> 00:09:33.364
Seventeen years old
and already a prime target

00:09:33.406 --> 00:09:36.075
among football scouts,
Cristiano Ronaldo and Sporting

00:09:36.117 --> 00:09:39.370
faced off against football giant
Manchester United.

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:41.372
Old Trafford's a far cry
from the dirt pitches

00:09:41.414 --> 00:09:42.915
of Madeira, Portugal,

00:09:42.957 --> 00:09:45.042
and The Red Devils
are football icons.

00:09:45.042 --> 00:09:46.877
Undaunted in front of
the legendary coach

00:09:46.877 --> 00:09:48.379
Sir Alex Ferguson,

00:09:48.421 --> 00:09:49.755
and giving the performance
of a lifetime,

00:09:49.797 --> 00:09:51.924
Sporting won 3-1.

00:09:51.966 --> 00:09:55.970
And Ronaldo was the only thing
that anyone could talk about.

00:09:56.012 --> 00:09:58.431
Manchester United was,
for me, I think

00:09:58.472 --> 00:10:00.141
that was his stepping-stone

00:10:00.182 --> 00:10:03.185
to move his career
much more forward.

00:10:03.227 --> 00:10:05.062
Ferguson saw something
there in a player

00:10:05.062 --> 00:10:08.232
that really could progress
and become something big.

00:10:08.232 --> 00:10:11.444
And of course we all know
today, that's what was the case.

00:10:11.485 --> 00:10:13.237
(narrator)
Ironically, it wasn't
the assistant coaches

00:10:13.237 --> 00:10:15.573
who had the idea to sign Ronaldo
to Manchester United.

00:10:15.615 --> 00:10:17.450
It was the players.

00:10:17.491 --> 00:10:19.577
On the way home from the match,
a few of his would-be teammates

00:10:19.577 --> 00:10:21.704
convinced Ferguson
that Ronaldo should be

00:10:21.746 --> 00:10:22.872
on their side.

00:10:22.913 --> 00:10:24.999
But other clubs
had taken notice

00:10:25.041 --> 00:10:26.626
of the teenage phenomenon.

00:10:26.667 --> 00:10:28.252
Ronaldo's path
to Manchester United

00:10:28.252 --> 00:10:30.463
was almost derailed
by Arsenal's manager

00:10:30.504 --> 00:10:32.423
Arsene Wegner.

00:10:32.465 --> 00:10:34.675
In fact, Ronaldo was so close
to signing with the Gunners,

00:10:34.717 --> 00:10:36.927
Wegner gave Ronaldo
his own number 9 jersey.

00:10:36.927 --> 00:10:41.390
But Ferguson was able to snatch
the Portuguese star.

00:10:41.432 --> 00:10:43.267
Remember, he came in
as a 17-year-old lad

00:10:43.267 --> 00:10:45.770
and really developed himself
here as a great footballer,

00:10:45.811 --> 00:10:48.147
so I think we
are proud of that.

00:10:48.189 --> 00:10:49.440
(narrator)
Never one to mince his words,

00:10:49.482 --> 00:10:51.108
Ferguson was a visionary

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:53.277
who led one of the world's
best football clubs

00:10:53.277 --> 00:10:55.112
for over two decades.

00:10:55.154 --> 00:10:57.281
He brought home 38 trophies,

00:10:57.281 --> 00:10:59.659
including 13 Premier
League Titles.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:02.453
The training session,
intensity, expectation,

00:11:02.495 --> 00:11:05.623
the level of concentration

00:11:05.623 --> 00:11:07.667
will always manifest itself
in a Saturday.

00:11:07.708 --> 00:11:10.628
He's had
a amazing career, um...

00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:14.298
One that, you know,
many managers look at

00:11:14.298 --> 00:11:18.052
and want to achieve
what he has achieved.

00:11:18.094 --> 00:11:22.014
(David Beckham)
I owe him a lot
as a manager for the way

00:11:22.056 --> 00:11:24.642
he brought me
into Manchester United,

00:11:24.642 --> 00:11:27.144
and then he groomed me
into a player

00:11:27.144 --> 00:11:30.815
that went on
to win 19 trophies.

00:11:30.815 --> 00:11:32.566
(narrator)
Upon his arrival,

00:11:32.608 --> 00:11:35.152
it was requested that Ronaldo
wear a special jersey.

00:11:35.152 --> 00:11:37.154
Cristiano Ronaldo would don

00:11:37.196 --> 00:11:39.657
the heavily weighted
number 7.

00:11:39.699 --> 00:11:43.744
And as time would tell,
he would immortalize it.

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:54.672
(Paul Cann)
So, you're looking
for a father figure

00:11:54.714 --> 00:11:57.007
to look after you
and take you under your wings,

00:11:57.007 --> 00:11:58.718
and you as a player

00:11:58.759 --> 00:12:01.554
would need to trust
that particular person.

00:12:01.595 --> 00:12:03.723
And that's obviously
what happened.

00:12:03.764 --> 00:12:05.933
And when you've got a manager
like Sir Alex Ferguson

00:12:05.975 --> 00:12:08.352
and the background staff,
and the players of course,

00:12:08.352 --> 00:12:09.729
help him to settle,

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:11.439
that would allow him
then to

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:13.023
freely play his football.

00:12:13.023 --> 00:12:15.609
(narrator)
Ronaldo signed with United

00:12:15.651 --> 00:12:20.364
for a transfer fee
of an extraordinary
15 million Euros.

00:12:20.364 --> 00:12:22.366
You've got a manager that's
been there for 20-odd years

00:12:22.366 --> 00:12:25.745
that had won pretty much,
well, everything in the game.

00:12:25.786 --> 00:12:29.832
Unbelievable success record.

00:12:29.874 --> 00:12:32.042
(translator)
I think it's just
the way I play.

00:12:32.084 --> 00:12:33.878
Ever since I was
a youngster in Madeira,

00:12:33.919 --> 00:12:36.255
I've always been a player
that enjoyed

00:12:36.297 --> 00:12:38.382
taking someone
on one-on-one.

00:12:38.382 --> 00:12:41.594
It's in my nature,
and I've always done this.

00:12:41.635 --> 00:12:42.887
He's speedy with the ball,
either foot,

00:12:42.928 --> 00:12:45.222
manipulating it,
making decisions

00:12:45.222 --> 00:12:47.099
in and outside
of fullback,

00:12:47.141 --> 00:12:49.769
planning and moving into
position and done at speed.

00:12:49.810 --> 00:12:51.729
And everything
was done at great speed.

00:12:51.771 --> 00:12:55.816
And I think that was the thing
that made me sit up.

00:12:55.858 --> 00:12:57.943
(narrator)
Ronaldo wasn't the first
young football star

00:12:57.985 --> 00:13:00.780
to join Manchester
and wear the number seven.

00:13:00.821 --> 00:13:03.407
David Beckham began his career
with the Red Devils

00:13:03.407 --> 00:13:05.576
at the age of just 17.

00:13:05.576 --> 00:13:07.912
Beckham was to quickly
fulfill his potential

00:13:07.953 --> 00:13:09.955
as one of the world's best,

00:13:09.997 --> 00:13:12.291
winning six league titles
and two FA cups

00:13:12.333 --> 00:13:13.918
at the hallowed
grounds of Old Trafford.

00:13:13.918 --> 00:13:15.586
He always had
a lovely smile, you know,

00:13:15.628 --> 00:13:17.588
and he always presents
himself well,

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:21.592
but as a young kid, when I
got him at 12 years of age,

00:13:21.592 --> 00:13:25.429
his great desire was to be
the best footballer.

00:13:25.429 --> 00:13:28.349
He was a fantastic trainer,
practiced all the time.

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:30.434
And at nighttime, he'd
come back with the schoolboys

00:13:30.434 --> 00:13:31.811
and practice with them.

00:13:31.852 --> 00:13:33.604
(narrator)
Much like Ronaldo,

00:13:33.604 --> 00:13:36.106
Beckham has played the role
of hero and villain.

00:13:36.148 --> 00:13:40.236
In a 1998 World Cup second-round
match against Argentina,

00:13:40.277 --> 00:13:41.904
Beckham, after being fouled,

00:13:41.946 --> 00:13:45.449
kicked midfielder
Diego Simeone in the calf.

00:13:45.449 --> 00:13:50.246
Beckham was given a red card
and England was eliminated.

00:13:50.287 --> 00:13:51.789
Beckham was blamed
for the defeat,

00:13:51.831 --> 00:13:53.374
and he and his family
received death threats.

00:13:53.415 --> 00:13:55.459
He was demonized
in the media.

00:13:55.459 --> 00:14:00.464
Crazed fans hung and burned
an effigy of him outside a pub.

00:14:00.464 --> 00:14:02.967
You'd much rather
have your own fans--

00:14:02.967 --> 00:14:05.594
you do expect a lot of stick
from opposition fans,

00:14:05.636 --> 00:14:08.180
but you'd much rather
have your own fans with you

00:14:08.222 --> 00:14:10.099
than against you.

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:13.394
And fans help much more
when you're having a bad time.

00:14:13.435 --> 00:14:15.020
It's easy to cheer,

00:14:15.062 --> 00:14:16.689
to cheer your team
when you're doing well,

00:14:16.730 --> 00:14:18.190
but when you're having
a bit of a rough time,

00:14:18.232 --> 00:14:20.776
you need your fans
to get through it.

00:14:20.818 --> 00:14:23.195
Beckham's the link,
if you like,

00:14:23.237 --> 00:14:25.030
with these players
in the countries

00:14:25.072 --> 00:14:28.158
then there's a good chance
that he may come over, Ronaldo,

00:14:28.158 --> 00:14:32.496
to participate
in the US League, the MLS.

00:14:32.496 --> 00:14:35.165
And if he does, I certainly
think that that would be

00:14:35.207 --> 00:14:37.418
a huge coup for the US.

00:14:37.459 --> 00:14:40.170
I'm excited about bringing
the team and being part

00:14:40.170 --> 00:14:43.007
of the MLS and continuing
to be a part of the MLS.

00:14:44.884 --> 00:14:46.510
(narrator)
Cristiano Ronaldo's
United career

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:48.178
proved to be successful
from the get-go.

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:50.681
In his first season,
Ronaldo scored the opening goal

00:14:50.723 --> 00:14:54.476
in United's 3-0 FA Cup final
victory over Millwall.

00:14:54.518 --> 00:14:55.895
The first ever
Portuguese footballer

00:14:55.936 --> 00:14:57.855
to play for Manchester United,

00:14:57.897 --> 00:15:00.232
Cristiano Ronaldo
had not only arrived,

00:15:00.274 --> 00:15:03.861
but also became
Player of the Year.

00:15:03.903 --> 00:15:06.363
Ronaldo is heralded
as a master striker.

00:15:06.363 --> 00:15:09.450
He plays an attacking role
better than anyone,

00:15:09.491 --> 00:15:12.328
often referred to as
"The Sultan of the Step-over,"

00:15:12.369 --> 00:15:14.246
showing unmatched skill
with both feet

00:15:14.288 --> 00:15:16.540
and the ability
to beat players one-on-one

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:19.084
unparalleled in the rest
of the game.

00:15:19.126 --> 00:15:21.378
The whole game
of the football has changed.

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:23.088
It's completely changed.

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:24.632
You know, you've got
all this different dietician-y

00:15:24.673 --> 00:15:26.842
type of food that you
have to eat now,

00:15:26.884 --> 00:15:29.887
and they monitor
your heart rate,

00:15:29.887 --> 00:15:31.931
your pulse rate,
everything.

00:15:31.972 --> 00:15:33.807
(narrator)
His height, strength,
and vertical leap

00:15:33.849 --> 00:15:35.809
give him an edge
in aerial challenges,

00:15:35.851 --> 00:15:38.270
and the majority of his goals
are, in fact, headers.

00:15:38.312 --> 00:15:41.023
I think he's been a fantastic
advert for the game.

00:15:41.065 --> 00:15:44.276
His scoring record,
ratio to games played,

00:15:44.318 --> 00:15:45.444
is second to none.

00:15:45.486 --> 00:15:48.989
Ronaldo, tremendous player.

00:15:49.031 --> 00:15:50.407
One of the best players
in the world,

00:15:50.449 --> 00:15:53.661
if not the best
goal-scorer in the world.

00:15:53.702 --> 00:15:58.499
And when he scores goals...
left foot, right foot,

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:00.584
he can head a ball,

00:16:00.584 --> 00:16:02.962
he can take people on,
his step-overs.

00:16:03.003 --> 00:16:04.088
(narrator)
At the height of his success

00:16:04.129 --> 00:16:06.590
at Manchester United
in 2005,

00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:08.467
Ronaldo was dealt
a significant blow.

00:16:08.509 --> 00:16:10.427
His father passed away.

00:16:10.427 --> 00:16:12.763
Jose died due to a chronic
liver condition

00:16:12.805 --> 00:16:16.308
brought on by years of
struggling against alcoholism.

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:18.852
He was only 52 years old.

00:16:18.894 --> 00:16:22.606
Ronaldo, only 20 at the time,
was hit hard by the loss.

00:16:22.606 --> 00:16:24.608
But, as at every moment
of hardship in his life,

00:16:24.608 --> 00:16:27.277
Ronaldo's mother Maria
was there for him.

00:16:27.277 --> 00:16:31.615
She's been an unwavering pillar
of support and love in his life,

00:16:31.615 --> 00:16:33.784
and he's said often
that he would not be

00:16:33.784 --> 00:16:38.247
where he is today
without his mother.

00:16:38.288 --> 00:16:40.624
Ronaldo still carries
a lingering heartache

00:16:40.624 --> 00:16:43.460
for his father's passing,
as he never got to share

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:45.629
any of his success
with his father.

00:16:45.629 --> 00:16:48.590
To this day he never forgets
how his dad was instrumental

00:16:48.632 --> 00:16:51.802
in getting him started
in this sport.

00:16:51.844 --> 00:16:55.014
Many think him
too much of a peacock,

00:16:55.055 --> 00:16:56.640
preening and flashy,

00:16:56.640 --> 00:16:58.308
concerned completely
with his image.

00:16:58.308 --> 00:17:01.145
He doesn't make it easy,
turning many viewers off

00:17:01.145 --> 00:17:03.647
with his arrogance
and over-confidence.

00:17:03.647 --> 00:17:05.566
Where I think
he's toned it down, I think,

00:17:05.607 --> 00:17:07.818
by hanging with models
and other sports stars

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:09.987
that are on the kind
of salary that he's on,

00:17:10.029 --> 00:17:13.157
um, it has taught him a lot
for how to, you know,

00:17:13.157 --> 00:17:17.202
look good,
but keep it minimum,
which he's never done well.

00:17:17.244 --> 00:17:20.164
He loves the bling-bling,
he loves the solid tan.

00:17:20.164 --> 00:17:24.209
But I think he's learned a lot
and he's matured a lot.

00:17:24.251 --> 00:17:26.295
And that's seen
through his fashion

00:17:26.336 --> 00:17:28.297
and his clothing choices.

00:17:28.338 --> 00:17:30.340
The guy
is a total professional.

00:17:30.382 --> 00:17:33.343
What he does in his own time
is up to him, I mean, that's--

00:17:33.343 --> 00:17:36.180
He is obviously,
I think he gives quite

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:39.808
a good image
for a footballer.

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:41.351
(narrator)
Other fans think he dives

00:17:41.393 --> 00:17:43.020
without the slightest
contact,

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:44.897
and are annoyed that a player
as well built as Ronaldo

00:17:44.938 --> 00:17:47.024
would take
to the turf so easily.

00:17:47.066 --> 00:17:49.818
Ronaldo's penchant
for persuading referees

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:53.697
was highlighted in a 2006
World Cup match against England.

00:17:53.697 --> 00:17:56.033
Wayne Rooney,
a Manchester United teammate,

00:17:56.033 --> 00:17:59.078
was whistled for stamping
on a Portugal defender.

00:17:59.119 --> 00:18:03.165
Ronaldo immediately started
to plead his case to the ref

00:18:03.207 --> 00:18:04.541
and Rooney shoved him.

00:18:04.541 --> 00:18:06.376
Rooney was given
the red card.

00:18:06.376 --> 00:18:08.128
And as he left the pitch,

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:11.256
cameras caught Ronaldo winking
at his teammate.

00:18:11.298 --> 00:18:13.717
Portugal may have won
the quarterfinal match,

00:18:13.717 --> 00:18:16.386
but Ronaldo didn't win many fans
in the process.

00:18:16.386 --> 00:18:18.430
(woman)
Somebody's probably
gonna break your legs,

00:18:18.472 --> 00:18:20.891
in a--
in a nasty tackle.

00:18:20.933 --> 00:18:22.851
Could be Rooney,
you never know.

00:18:22.893 --> 00:18:25.729
You think?

00:18:25.729 --> 00:18:29.274
He's got, he's got to get you
back for one, doesn't he?

00:18:29.316 --> 00:18:32.402
(narrator)
Rumors of turmoil
began to spread

00:18:32.444 --> 00:18:34.238
that tension between
Ronaldo and Rooney

00:18:34.238 --> 00:18:36.073
following
the now infamous wink

00:18:36.073 --> 00:18:38.575
would be too much for
Manchester United to overcome.

00:18:38.617 --> 00:18:41.662
Ronaldo was taking the brunt
of the blame.

00:18:41.703 --> 00:18:44.081
CR7, as he was known,

00:18:44.081 --> 00:18:46.667
was becoming football's
greatest villain.

00:18:49.294 --> 00:18:51.296
(narrator)
Soon, reports surfaced
that Ronaldo wanted to transfer,

00:18:51.338 --> 00:18:53.757
and Real Madrid
was his chosen team.

00:18:53.757 --> 00:18:57.886
He had to get there by going
through Manchester United,

00:18:57.928 --> 00:18:59.930
and the progression
that he made through that club

00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:02.099
enabled him then
to move forward

00:19:02.141 --> 00:19:04.643
into a Real Madrid team

00:19:04.685 --> 00:19:08.438
that today is huge.

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:10.774
And that's the club
that he wanted to go to.

00:19:10.774 --> 00:19:13.443
His family, I think, wanted him
to go to that club, as well.

00:19:13.485 --> 00:19:16.530
His mother, and he was
in a situation

00:19:16.572 --> 00:19:18.448
where he couldn't say no.

00:19:18.448 --> 00:19:19.992
(narrator)
The press told stories
of a torn locker room,

00:19:20.033 --> 00:19:21.952
and the team's chemistry
in jeopardy.

00:19:21.952 --> 00:19:24.746
No one could blame
Ronaldo if he left.

00:19:24.788 --> 00:19:27.624
He could've blamed it on the fan
reaction, the resentment.

00:19:27.624 --> 00:19:30.127
He had a built-in excuse

00:19:30.169 --> 00:19:33.672
in that the World Cup incident
was too much to overcome.

00:19:33.714 --> 00:19:36.800
But Cristiano Ronaldo
rarely takes the easy route.

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:39.720
(translator)
There are things in life
that deserve no comment.

00:19:39.761 --> 00:19:42.764
This is one more of those
that will receive no comment

00:19:42.806 --> 00:19:44.808
on my part,
for obvious reasons.

00:19:44.808 --> 00:19:48.937
I've always respected all
my coaches everywhere I've been,

00:19:48.979 --> 00:19:51.148
and I always keep
the positive things.

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:53.317
So I always try to learn
something new from them.

00:19:53.358 --> 00:19:55.152
To talk about people
that speak ill of me,

00:19:55.152 --> 00:19:57.487
well, it's not something
that I'm used to.

00:19:57.487 --> 00:19:59.823
People talk ill of me,
especially in Portugal.

00:19:59.823 --> 00:20:01.992
But I don't spit into the plate
that I eat from.

00:20:02.034 --> 00:20:04.328
Does he understand that?
Is that correct?

00:20:04.369 --> 00:20:06.288
I just try to keep
to the positive things.

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:07.748
If you watch the players,
the first thing they want

00:20:07.789 --> 00:20:09.166
to do at the end
of the game is go across

00:20:09.208 --> 00:20:11.919
to their own supporters
and thank them.

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:15.631
But on the other hand,
you've got other clubs where,

00:20:15.672 --> 00:20:19.384
if things aren't
working out, then the fans
can turn on you very quick.

00:20:19.426 --> 00:20:22.596
And that's why he's got
as far as he has done today,
by playing for Real Madrid,

00:20:22.638 --> 00:20:26.308
because of his arrogance,
his professionalism.

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:28.352
(narrator)
Ronaldo met manager
Sir Alex Ferguson

00:20:28.352 --> 00:20:31.855
for dinner in Portugal
to discuss the situation.

00:20:31.855 --> 00:20:34.816
Sir Alex is no stranger
to handling football superstars,

00:20:34.858 --> 00:20:37.986
and convinced the young
striker to stay.

00:20:38.028 --> 00:20:40.864
A five-year extension
was inked, and Ronaldo became

00:20:40.864 --> 00:20:44.576
the highest paid player
in the team's history.

00:20:44.618 --> 00:20:46.536
They are more or less
film stars, movie stars.

00:20:46.536 --> 00:20:49.039
The amount of money that's
poured into the game now has--

00:20:49.081 --> 00:20:52.376
has risen their status
massively.

00:20:52.376 --> 00:20:54.544
(narrator)
On the heels of his
new five-year deal,

00:20:54.586 --> 00:20:58.340
Ronaldo carried the Red Devils
to its second of what would be

00:20:58.382 --> 00:21:01.218
three straight English
Premier League championships,

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:04.888
as well as taking home the UEFA
Champions League trophy.

00:21:04.888 --> 00:21:08.850
I just try to do
my best all the time,
season by season.

00:21:08.892 --> 00:21:12.187
I try to, to be better,
better player, better person.

00:21:12.229 --> 00:21:15.691
I try to learn myself
all the time.

00:21:15.732 --> 00:21:18.860
And, um, I have opportunity
to score goals and I score.

00:21:18.902 --> 00:21:21.780
(narrator)
One of the gems
of Ferguson's legendary career

00:21:21.822 --> 00:21:26.785
was keeping Ronaldo
in a United uniform
for as long as he did.

00:21:26.827 --> 00:21:31.290
Ferguson was known
for cultivating talent
as well as clashing with it.

00:21:31.331 --> 00:21:33.917
Tensions between Ferguson
and David Beckham

00:21:33.917 --> 00:21:35.627
boiled over in 2003,

00:21:35.669 --> 00:21:38.755
when following a loss
to Arsenal in the FA cup,

00:21:38.797 --> 00:21:40.924
Ferguson kicked a boot
at David Beckham,

00:21:40.924 --> 00:21:44.094
resulting in the Englishman
getting stitches above his eye.

00:21:44.136 --> 00:21:45.929
David did not have
two stitches put in his head,

00:21:45.929 --> 00:21:47.931
he had no stitches.

00:21:47.931 --> 00:21:51.893
So it was a graze, and he's
dealt with, with a doctor,

00:21:51.935 --> 00:21:55.063
there's no problem,
and we move on.

00:21:55.105 --> 00:21:56.440
(narrator)
And similar to Beckham,

00:21:56.481 --> 00:21:58.442
Ronaldo eventually
was granted his request

00:21:58.442 --> 00:22:02.446
to transfer to Real Madrid
in 2009.

00:22:02.487 --> 00:22:06.616
The £80 million transfer fee
was a record at that time.

00:22:06.616 --> 00:22:08.577
I think we have a player
in the top of his game.

00:22:08.618 --> 00:22:11.455
We have a player
that left Portugal

00:22:11.455 --> 00:22:13.749
with an incredible talent,

00:22:13.790 --> 00:22:15.917
transformed
that incredible talent

00:22:15.959 --> 00:22:18.128
in his time in Manchester.

00:22:18.128 --> 00:22:20.797
And now knowing
a certain coach,

00:22:20.797 --> 00:22:23.467
I think he achieved
his maximum level.

00:22:23.508 --> 00:22:26.636
He's fabulous player.

00:22:26.678 --> 00:22:30.057
And normally this kind
of players, they make,

00:22:30.098 --> 00:22:32.142
uh, they can
make a difference.

00:22:32.142 --> 00:22:33.310
(narrator)
That's until current teammate

00:22:33.352 --> 00:22:34.811
Gareth Bale joined Madrid

00:22:34.853 --> 00:22:36.438
transferring over
from Tottenham

00:22:36.480 --> 00:22:37.606
in the Barclay's
Premier League.

00:22:37.647 --> 00:22:39.483
Our guys
is doing amazing.

00:22:39.524 --> 00:22:43.195
He start a little bit...

00:22:43.236 --> 00:22:46.281
As I say, like with some
injuries, some small problems,

00:22:46.323 --> 00:22:49.493
it's normal because
he didn't do the preseason,

00:22:49.534 --> 00:22:51.578
and after what's happened
with him,

00:22:51.620 --> 00:22:53.497
a lot
of pressure, you know.

00:22:53.497 --> 00:22:55.874
It's hard, but I think
now he's in a good way.

00:22:55.916 --> 00:22:59.336
He helps out a lot,
he's integrate more in the team.

00:22:59.336 --> 00:23:02.839
People like him,
like the supporters

00:23:02.881 --> 00:23:05.509
and the players
around him.

00:23:05.509 --> 00:23:07.427
I think it's a--
it's a fantastic player,

00:23:07.469 --> 00:23:11.348
and I wish that he can
help us win trophies.

00:23:11.348 --> 00:23:14.017
Cristiano Ronaldo is, for me,
the best player in the world.

00:23:14.017 --> 00:23:15.852
I think he's a massive factor.

00:23:15.894 --> 00:23:18.647
Why I wanted
to come here as well.

00:23:18.688 --> 00:23:21.942
I think the team is full
of world-class players

00:23:21.983 --> 00:23:24.694
and there comes
no better than him.

00:23:24.694 --> 00:23:27.155
And, uh, it will obviously
be an honor.

00:23:28.698 --> 00:23:30.033
(narrator)
At first, everyone wondered

00:23:30.033 --> 00:23:32.369
if these two could play
together in harmony.

00:23:32.411 --> 00:23:35.372
It's not difficult for him,
but I understand.

00:23:35.414 --> 00:23:37.416
If you, if you speak
with him, you can see

00:23:37.457 --> 00:23:39.543
that he's very
exciting to play,

00:23:39.543 --> 00:23:42.379
to help the team, to getting
better and better.

00:23:42.379 --> 00:23:44.256
But it's better
to leave him alone.

00:23:44.297 --> 00:23:46.425
Don't make him pressure,
do pressure to another players.

00:23:46.466 --> 00:23:47.717
Leave him alone.

00:23:47.717 --> 00:23:49.386
Because I'm sure 100%

00:23:49.386 --> 00:23:52.514
that he's gonna
do well for the club.

00:23:52.556 --> 00:23:55.392
He gonna help us a lot
because he's a fantastic player.

00:23:55.434 --> 00:23:58.228
He's a fantastic boy,
and he always want to learn.

00:23:58.228 --> 00:24:00.397
And this is
the most important.

00:24:00.397 --> 00:24:02.691
(narrator)
Now, after the first season,

00:24:02.732 --> 00:24:04.734
the combination
of Ronaldo and Bale

00:24:04.776 --> 00:24:08.905
is proving to be deadly
for any opposing team.

00:24:08.905 --> 00:24:12.534
Cristiano Ronaldo soon
became a worldwide phenomenon.

00:24:12.576 --> 00:24:16.246
He's the most Google-searched
athlete across the globe.

00:24:16.288 --> 00:24:19.916
Millions idolize him,
and just as many hate him.

00:24:19.958 --> 00:24:23.170
He is the ultimate polarizing
figure in sports.

00:24:25.088 --> 00:24:27.716
I think that Ronaldo coming
from a very poor background

00:24:27.757 --> 00:24:30.886
has indeed had an effect
on his career

00:24:30.927 --> 00:24:33.263
and on his
business decisions.

00:24:33.305 --> 00:24:37.684
I think that he has
had to claw his way up

00:24:37.726 --> 00:24:40.228
and take every opportunity
that's given to him,

00:24:40.270 --> 00:24:42.063
but equally, so too

00:24:42.105 --> 00:24:43.315
have other people
that have come

00:24:43.356 --> 00:24:45.859
from much better-off
backgrounds.

00:24:45.901 --> 00:24:48.987
But I think he's been
very clever in the way

00:24:49.029 --> 00:24:52.866
that he's used
his perhaps skills

00:24:52.908 --> 00:24:57.287
that he learned at a young age
to his advantage today.

00:24:57.329 --> 00:24:59.289
(narrator)
Although much of Ronaldo's skill

00:24:59.289 --> 00:25:01.625
was shaped and molded
with his fiery determination

00:25:01.625 --> 00:25:04.127
and will and pure hard work,

00:25:04.127 --> 00:25:06.129
one wonders if this
otherworldly talent

00:25:06.129 --> 00:25:08.507
got an assist from destiny.

00:25:08.548 --> 00:25:10.634
Born on February 5th, 1985,

00:25:10.634 --> 00:25:13.220
under the Aquarian sun
and Leo moon,

00:25:13.261 --> 00:25:16.306
the stars lit
the path for Ronaldo,

00:25:16.306 --> 00:25:19.309
equipping him with
the relentless passion
to be great.

00:25:19.309 --> 00:25:21.811
Aquarians are brilliant
communicators.

00:25:21.811 --> 00:25:24.981
They work well with the media,
so they're an absolute gift

00:25:25.023 --> 00:25:28.276
to any corporate organization
trying to push their wares.

00:25:28.318 --> 00:25:31.154
And Ronaldo has made
many endorsements

00:25:31.154 --> 00:25:33.323
for most products
you can think of.

00:25:33.365 --> 00:25:35.325
(narrator)
Those born with an Aquarian sun

00:25:35.367 --> 00:25:38.036
can be enchanting
and often unhinged.

00:25:38.078 --> 00:25:40.830
The placement of Mars could tell
us that little Cristiano Ronaldo

00:25:40.872 --> 00:25:45.168
would become a man of action,
a self-sufficient born leader.

00:25:45.168 --> 00:25:47.504
It seems even the Cosmos
has made it their goal

00:25:47.504 --> 00:25:49.881
to see Ronaldo
armed with all the traits

00:25:49.923 --> 00:25:51.883
of a superior
athletic force.

00:25:51.925 --> 00:25:54.469
Ronaldo is a really
typical Aquarian.

00:25:54.511 --> 00:25:56.388
He just loves the limelight.

00:25:56.429 --> 00:25:59.349
And Ronaldo will always
want to succeed.

00:25:59.391 --> 00:26:02.519
He'll always want to be
number one, the best.

00:26:02.561 --> 00:26:05.689
And if money comes with it,
well, money comes with it.

00:26:05.689 --> 00:26:08.316
Aquarians can take it
or leave it with money.

00:26:08.358 --> 00:26:10.402
But when money really
comes to an Aquarian,

00:26:10.443 --> 00:26:14.864
it either comes big time,
or nothing at all.

00:26:14.906 --> 00:26:18.076
In Ronaldo's case,
he's made plenty in his life.

00:26:18.118 --> 00:26:20.704
(narrator)
But he's not the only one
in his family to gain fame.

00:26:20.745 --> 00:26:23.873
Ronaldo's older sister,
Catia Aveiro is a singer

00:26:23.873 --> 00:26:25.959
and signed a record deal
in 2013.

00:27:02.495 --> 00:27:05.832
Naturally, Ronaldo
has always been her biggest fan

00:27:05.874 --> 00:27:07.250
as she used to sing
around the house

00:27:07.250 --> 00:27:09.002
when they were younger.

00:27:09.044 --> 00:27:10.962
No matter where her career
takes her, Catia knows

00:27:11.004 --> 00:27:15.050
her younger brother will always
be there to support her dreams.

00:27:15.091 --> 00:27:18.011
As Ronaldo's
legions of fans grew,

00:27:18.053 --> 00:27:19.763
so did his critics.

00:27:19.763 --> 00:27:22.265
Ronaldo instantly
had a target on his back.

00:27:22.265 --> 00:27:23.850
Tabloid magazines
and websites

00:27:23.892 --> 00:27:25.935
hounded his every
move off the pitch.

00:27:25.977 --> 00:27:28.563
The word to describe
Cristiano Ronaldo... skimpy.

00:27:28.605 --> 00:27:30.273
Loves skimpy.

00:27:30.273 --> 00:27:31.941
Speedos, I don't get it.

00:27:31.983 --> 00:27:33.652
You know, I suppose
if you look that good

00:27:33.693 --> 00:27:35.945
you can show it off,
but he shows it off a lot.

00:27:35.945 --> 00:27:37.280
(narrator)
Any celebrity knows

00:27:37.280 --> 00:27:39.699
that as fame rises,
privacy often falls.

00:27:39.741 --> 00:27:41.826
Paparazzi are an issue
for any star,

00:27:41.868 --> 00:27:45.580
but for a global
icon like Ronaldo,

00:27:45.622 --> 00:27:48.375
it can be impossible to find
a moment's peace.

00:27:48.416 --> 00:27:50.585
(man)
Watch out, watch out, watch out!

00:27:50.627 --> 00:27:53.880
Yo, you're going the wrong way.
You're going the wrong way.

00:27:53.922 --> 00:27:55.465
Back up!

00:27:55.465 --> 00:27:56.800
(man #2)
What are you doing here?

00:27:56.841 --> 00:27:58.301
- Back up!
- Cristiano!

00:27:58.301 --> 00:28:00.261
(shouting)

00:28:00.303 --> 00:28:01.638
(narrator)
His home is stalked

00:28:01.680 --> 00:28:03.098
by cameramen
and videographers,

00:28:03.139 --> 00:28:05.141
often provoking him
with personal questions.

00:28:05.141 --> 00:28:06.518
(men shouting)

00:28:06.559 --> 00:28:08.395
(man)
How's your baby?!

00:28:08.436 --> 00:28:09.979
(narrator)
And Ronaldo has clashed

00:28:09.979 --> 00:28:12.148
with a paparazzo on more
than one occasion.

00:28:12.190 --> 00:28:14.150
It's hard to blame him
considering how much

00:28:14.150 --> 00:28:16.194
they hawk
his every single move.

00:28:16.236 --> 00:28:17.654
I think the difference
with the Beckhams

00:28:17.696 --> 00:28:19.614
is that they're
a partnership.

00:28:19.656 --> 00:28:22.659
There's one of Ronaldo,
there's two Beckhams.

00:28:22.701 --> 00:28:24.953
They weren't the people
that arrived on the scene

00:28:24.994 --> 00:28:26.496
many years ago.

00:28:26.538 --> 00:28:29.666
Ronaldo I think is equally
making that effort,

00:28:29.666 --> 00:28:31.835
but he comes from
a very different culture,

00:28:31.835 --> 00:28:34.003
a very, very different
way of life.

00:28:34.003 --> 00:28:35.505
(narrator)
However, his salary does allow

00:28:35.547 --> 00:28:38.508
the striker to outrun
the paps.

00:28:38.550 --> 00:28:40.176
The footballer
has some of the fastest

00:28:40.218 --> 00:28:42.262
and most expensive cars
on the planet.

00:28:42.303 --> 00:28:44.889
Whether he's whipping
by in his Bugatti Veyron,

00:28:44.931 --> 00:28:47.183
or cruising in his
Rolls Royce Phantom,

00:28:47.225 --> 00:28:51.354
he has spent nearly $5 million
on his treasured car collection.

00:28:51.354 --> 00:28:54.107
Cristiano Ronaldo is one of
the highest paid sportsman

00:28:54.149 --> 00:28:56.568
in the world, so you can
imagine he's gonna have

00:28:56.609 --> 00:28:59.279
one of the best
collections in the world.

00:28:59.320 --> 00:29:02.365
I mean, you can start off,
he's got a Bugatti Veyron,

00:29:02.365 --> 00:29:05.201
he's got plenty
of Lamborghinis, McLarens,

00:29:05.201 --> 00:29:07.746
Ferraris, Bentleys,

00:29:07.787 --> 00:29:10.540
pretty much anything
you can imagine,

00:29:10.582 --> 00:29:12.751
Cristiano Ronaldo will have.

00:29:12.792 --> 00:29:15.378
The lifestyle is fantastic.

00:29:15.378 --> 00:29:17.464
There is money,
there are cars,

00:29:17.505 --> 00:29:19.841
there are houses,
media exposure.

00:29:19.883 --> 00:29:22.302
It's very difficult to live
a life in the limelight,

00:29:22.343 --> 00:29:25.472
and that's why I think you see
a lot of the younger stars

00:29:25.513 --> 00:29:27.891
sort of failing,
as it would be,

00:29:27.932 --> 00:29:31.978
in many aspects of life
by the time they're mid-20's.

00:29:32.020 --> 00:29:34.397
He likes to be seen,
he's got a lot of convertibles,

00:29:34.397 --> 00:29:36.733
so he'll pop the roof
and people, you know,

00:29:36.775 --> 00:29:38.902
he wants people to see him
driving these cars.

00:29:38.943 --> 00:29:41.654
And that's part
of his character.

00:29:41.696 --> 00:29:42.697
(narrator)
But he doesn't only fill

00:29:42.739 --> 00:29:44.699
his own garage.

00:29:44.741 --> 00:29:47.327
Ronaldo promised the five-person
training staff of Real Madrid

00:29:47.368 --> 00:29:49.746
that if he won
the FIFA Ballon d'Or,

00:29:49.746 --> 00:29:53.958
he would buy each of them
a new car of their choice.

00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:56.252
In 2013, Ronaldo went home
with the award,

00:29:56.294 --> 00:29:57.545
and true to his word,

00:29:57.587 --> 00:29:59.422
his training staff
was driving home

00:29:59.422 --> 00:30:03.259
in their brand-new cars
soon after.

00:30:03.259 --> 00:30:05.762
Cannot expect a better night
than this one ever in my dreams,

00:30:05.804 --> 00:30:09.349
so I have to be proud
of my work,

00:30:09.390 --> 00:30:11.726
what I did during the year.

00:30:11.768 --> 00:30:15.313
And this is gonna
give me motivation

00:30:15.355 --> 00:30:19.609
to work more, and dedicate
myself more for the future.

00:30:19.651 --> 00:30:22.612
And I hope to be here next year
to try to win the third one.

00:30:22.654 --> 00:30:24.113
(narrator)
Throughout his career,

00:30:24.155 --> 00:30:26.783
Ronaldo made headlines
on and off the pitch.

00:30:26.825 --> 00:30:29.911
Recently, he announced
that there is a junior Ronaldo.

00:30:29.953 --> 00:30:32.789
The identity of the mother
has never been released.

00:30:32.789 --> 00:30:35.625
The boy,
named Cristiano Ronaldo Jr.

00:30:35.625 --> 00:30:38.920
attends every match
with his grandmother.

00:30:38.962 --> 00:30:41.464
Ronaldo says he plans to
raise him with religious values

00:30:41.464 --> 00:30:43.174
and won't spoil him

00:30:43.216 --> 00:30:45.635
even though he's being
raised in immense wealth.

00:30:45.677 --> 00:30:47.637
Ronaldo prides himself
on being

00:30:47.637 --> 00:30:50.473
a loving and caring dad.

00:30:50.473 --> 00:30:53.309
Ronaldo, despite his
gargantuan wealth and success,

00:30:53.351 --> 00:30:55.311
is always mindful of where
he came from,

00:30:55.353 --> 00:30:58.690
and the hardships he had
to endure to achieve his dreams.

00:30:58.731 --> 00:31:00.567
The asphalt alley
and stone well

00:31:00.608 --> 00:31:02.569
are never far
from his thoughts.

00:31:02.610 --> 00:31:04.487
If you're looking for Ronaldo

00:31:04.487 --> 00:31:07.490
on his day off, you probably
won't find him in a local bar.

00:31:07.490 --> 00:31:10.326
Odds are he could be at a youth
practice in his native Portugal.

00:31:10.368 --> 00:31:12.495
Hello, hello.

00:31:12.495 --> 00:31:14.747
We pass, pass, pass, pass,
and we didn't shoot.

00:31:14.789 --> 00:31:18.001
One opportunity,
shoot in the net.

00:31:28.511 --> 00:31:31.389
I think they play
all in the same place.

00:31:31.431 --> 00:31:33.349
They have to make
this space huge.

00:31:36.060 --> 00:31:39.355
Try to be fast, try to,
you know, to fake him,

00:31:39.397 --> 00:31:42.025
and try to change
acceleration.

00:31:42.066 --> 00:31:44.235
Just try to have the ball.

00:31:44.277 --> 00:31:46.029
And good control.

00:31:46.029 --> 00:31:47.196
Good control.

00:31:51.659 --> 00:31:52.702
Good.

00:31:56.831 --> 00:31:58.708
(narrator)
Cristiano Ronaldo
has been criticized

00:31:58.708 --> 00:32:01.294
for his extravagant spending
and lifestyle.

00:32:01.336 --> 00:32:03.880
But without question,
his heart, support,

00:32:03.922 --> 00:32:06.758
and generosity
have saved many lives

00:32:06.799 --> 00:32:09.761
and given hope to those
that most need it.

00:32:12.096 --> 00:32:13.556
In December of 2004,

00:32:13.556 --> 00:32:17.060
Ronaldo's number 7
was a symbol of hope.

00:32:17.101 --> 00:32:19.062
An earthquake off the coast
of Indonesia

00:32:19.062 --> 00:32:21.648
caused one of the most
catastrophic tsunamis

00:32:21.689 --> 00:32:23.566
in recorded history.

00:32:23.566 --> 00:32:26.486
A six-year-old Acehnese
boy named Maltunis

00:32:26.527 --> 00:32:28.863
was swept out to sea
by the massive wave.

00:32:28.905 --> 00:32:31.574
Maltunis was carried
into a mangrove swamp.

00:32:31.574 --> 00:32:34.577
All he had to survive on
was rainwater in puddles,

00:32:34.577 --> 00:32:36.245
and packets of dried noodles

00:32:36.245 --> 00:32:38.122
that had washed up
in the wave.

00:32:38.164 --> 00:32:41.584
He was alone like this for
19 days before he was rescued

00:32:41.584 --> 00:32:45.505
and reunited with his father
and grandfather.

00:32:45.546 --> 00:32:48.132
News agencies
broadcasted images of Maltunis

00:32:48.174 --> 00:32:49.884
wearing a tattered
blood-stained,

00:32:49.926 --> 00:32:54.097
red football jersey,
with the number seven.

00:32:54.138 --> 00:32:56.265
The image of Maltunis
in that shirt went viral,

00:32:56.307 --> 00:32:58.351
as did his story.

00:32:58.393 --> 00:33:02.188
The young boy lost his mother
and sister in the tsunami.

00:33:02.230 --> 00:33:04.607
Touched and heartbroken,

00:33:04.607 --> 00:33:07.902
Ronaldo visited Maltunis
in Indonesia.

00:33:07.944 --> 00:33:09.278
He paid for
the boy's education,

00:33:09.320 --> 00:33:11.489
and made large donations
to rehabilitation

00:33:11.531 --> 00:33:14.450
and reconstruction
efforts for the community.

00:33:14.450 --> 00:33:15.785
Ronaldo also raised funds

00:33:15.785 --> 00:33:18.246
for an improved mangrove
forestation,

00:33:18.287 --> 00:33:21.541
a key element in helping
to save Maltunis' life

00:33:21.582 --> 00:33:24.794
during the aftermath
of this heart-wrenching event.

00:33:24.794 --> 00:33:27.463
♪

00:33:27.463 --> 00:33:29.632
Ronaldo's critics
perhaps ignore

00:33:29.632 --> 00:33:32.343
the star's many
philanthropic efforts.

00:33:32.385 --> 00:33:34.137
When Ronaldo found out
his biggest fan

00:33:34.137 --> 00:33:35.805
had life-threatening cancer,

00:33:35.805 --> 00:33:38.307
his world
stopped spinning.

00:33:38.349 --> 00:33:41.644
His mother was diagnosed
with breast cancer

00:33:41.644 --> 00:33:44.731
and fought through a series
of debilitating radiation

00:33:44.772 --> 00:33:46.816
treatments
to regain her health.

00:33:46.858 --> 00:33:50.319
Having seen her suffer,
Cristiano generously donated

00:33:50.319 --> 00:33:54.574
£100,000 to the hospital
that saved his mom's life.

00:33:54.615 --> 00:33:57.660
He continues to support
charities related to cancer

00:33:57.660 --> 00:34:00.663
and helped build a specialist
center at Hospital Central

00:34:00.663 --> 00:34:02.373
in his native Madeira.

00:34:02.415 --> 00:34:04.876
This past year,
Ronaldo received a letter

00:34:04.917 --> 00:34:08.046
from the family of 10-year-old
Erik Cruz Ortiz.

00:34:08.087 --> 00:34:11.340
The little Real Madrid
fan had a brain abnormality

00:34:11.382 --> 00:34:12.967
that required surgery,

00:34:13.009 --> 00:34:14.886
and the parents
were hoping Ronaldo would

00:34:14.927 --> 00:34:17.388
donate a jersey
and some shoes

00:34:17.430 --> 00:34:19.515
that they could auction off
to save money.

00:34:19.557 --> 00:34:22.143
Ronaldo went
a few steps further.

00:34:22.185 --> 00:34:25.438
He paid the £60,000
for the operation.

00:34:27.482 --> 00:34:29.192
Massive inspiration to--

00:34:29.233 --> 00:34:31.069
if you go back
home to Portugal,

00:34:31.110 --> 00:34:33.279
I mean, the whole
of the country love him.

00:34:33.321 --> 00:34:34.614
People don't know about

00:34:34.655 --> 00:34:36.866
the philanthropic work
that he does.

00:34:36.866 --> 00:34:39.702
A lot of his money goes
back into his home country.

00:34:39.702 --> 00:34:43.331
He's massively involved

00:34:43.372 --> 00:34:45.833
in the slums in Portugal.

00:34:45.875 --> 00:34:47.668
He's been doing lots
and lots of work there

00:34:47.710 --> 00:34:49.462
that people don't know about.

00:34:49.504 --> 00:34:51.214
(narrator)
Despite all his fame and wealth,

00:34:51.255 --> 00:34:55.051
no one can say that Ronaldo
is not a man of the people.

00:34:55.093 --> 00:34:57.887
During Real Madrid's 3-1
victory over Chelsea

00:34:57.887 --> 00:35:00.431
at the UEFA Champions
League friendly in Miami,

00:35:00.473 --> 00:35:04.560
a fan raced onto the pitch
to give Ronaldo a hug.

00:35:04.602 --> 00:35:06.938
(crowd cheering)

00:35:10.650 --> 00:35:12.610
I remember
holding him, saying,

00:35:12.652 --> 00:35:15.071
"Thank you, thank you,
thank you for this.

00:35:15.071 --> 00:35:16.614
"Thank you for
all you've done for me.

00:35:16.656 --> 00:35:18.241
"I wouldn't have been
where I am right now

00:35:18.282 --> 00:35:21.452
if I hadn't followed
you as a role model."

00:35:21.494 --> 00:35:25.331
I said, "I've always followed
you since 2005, 2006,

00:35:25.373 --> 00:35:27.625
before you were even
famous in Madrid."

00:35:27.667 --> 00:35:29.752
And I wish I had
the jersey, like I said,

00:35:29.752 --> 00:35:31.754
to show him that
I wasn't lying.

00:35:31.754 --> 00:35:34.423
It wasn't just for the fame,
I followed him for all,

00:35:34.423 --> 00:35:38.052
since he was a teenager
just like me, what I am now.

00:35:38.094 --> 00:35:39.637
When I knew he had
the potential.

00:35:39.679 --> 00:35:42.849
So I said, "I followed you,
you helped me in life

00:35:42.890 --> 00:35:47.061
"get through hard times because
I, just like you, Ronaldo,
"grew up with a single mom.

00:35:47.103 --> 00:35:49.772
"I never grew up
without a dad, either,
I know what it was like."

00:35:49.772 --> 00:35:51.607
And I think the moment
that really touched him,

00:35:51.649 --> 00:35:53.484
I said, in his ear,
and I remember whispering,

00:35:53.526 --> 00:35:55.570
not whispering, but telling
him in his ear, I said,

00:35:55.611 --> 00:35:58.781
"If I ever, ever had a father
figure to help me in my life,

00:35:58.781 --> 00:36:01.951
I always looked up to you
out of everyone in the world."

00:36:01.951 --> 00:36:04.453
Because of everything
he's done.

00:36:04.453 --> 00:36:06.664
His actions
on and off the soccer field.

00:36:06.706 --> 00:36:08.457
(narrator)
Ronaldo graciously chatted

00:36:08.457 --> 00:36:11.252
with the fan and walked
him off with security.

00:36:11.294 --> 00:36:13.129
But the story
didn't end there.

00:36:13.171 --> 00:36:15.423
Ronaldo wrote a letter
to the Florida judge

00:36:15.464 --> 00:36:17.967
asking for all criminal
charges to be dropped.

00:36:17.967 --> 00:36:20.970
I said to him, "Ronaldo,
you know, I followed
you and everything.

00:36:21.012 --> 00:36:25.558
Please, you know, please,
don't let the cops take me."

00:36:25.600 --> 00:36:27.268
And he said, "Don't worry,
I'm gonna take care of you."

00:36:27.310 --> 00:36:28.811
(narrator)
In the letter, Ronaldo wrote,

00:36:28.811 --> 00:36:31.606
"By all accounts he has
a bright future ahead of him,

00:36:31.647 --> 00:36:33.316
"and I'd hate see
this future ruined

00:36:33.316 --> 00:36:34.817
by an error of judgment."

00:36:34.817 --> 00:36:36.986
The charges were
dropped the next day.

00:36:40.323 --> 00:36:42.158
Cristiano is an athlete
who admittedly

00:36:42.158 --> 00:36:44.493
takes a lot of pride
in the way he looks.

00:36:44.535 --> 00:36:47.830
But after all, he does know
that it's all about branding.

00:36:47.830 --> 00:36:51.292
Ronaldo opened a boutique called
CR7 in his native Madeira,

00:36:51.334 --> 00:36:54.003
and another
in Lisbon in 2008.

00:36:54.003 --> 00:36:56.339
Last year, Ronaldo designed
his own undergarment line

00:36:56.380 --> 00:36:58.549
for men under the CR7 banner,

00:36:58.591 --> 00:37:00.676
giving his critics
plenty of ammunition.

00:37:00.718 --> 00:37:03.137
CR7 is the Cristiano
Ronaldo brand,

00:37:03.179 --> 00:37:05.556
and I think it's
very significant.

00:37:05.598 --> 00:37:08.476
I don't think it's as big
as Beckham, but then again,

00:37:08.517 --> 00:37:11.187
Beckham is the number one
known footballer in the world.

00:37:11.187 --> 00:37:15.524
Cristiano Ronaldo, I--
wasn't born into fashion,

00:37:15.566 --> 00:37:18.194
let's be real, because
in the early days

00:37:18.236 --> 00:37:20.529
when we saw him
with way too much hair gel,

00:37:20.529 --> 00:37:23.032
I mean Dippity-do was
like his go-to.

00:37:23.032 --> 00:37:25.409
It was just
to the extremes.

00:37:25.451 --> 00:37:28.537
He's used very block, bold
colors, which is very much

00:37:28.579 --> 00:37:33.000
Ronaldo's way of using
his fashion externally

00:37:33.042 --> 00:37:36.170
as well as internally
on his underpants and socks.

00:37:36.212 --> 00:37:38.714
To Beckham, there is no
comparison as footballers.

00:37:38.756 --> 00:37:41.092
Looks, Beckham,
well in front.

00:37:41.133 --> 00:37:44.053
Even though a lot of people
might have you think different.

00:37:44.053 --> 00:37:45.429
(narrator)
He didn't care.

00:37:45.471 --> 00:37:47.098
Profits experienced
a huge boost

00:37:47.139 --> 00:37:49.267
as his brand continues
to grow in record numbers.

00:37:49.308 --> 00:37:52.561
You have to be
in a situation where

00:37:52.561 --> 00:37:55.106
you are a role model
for the children,

00:37:55.147 --> 00:37:57.733
and so as long as they see
that that's what you are,

00:37:57.733 --> 00:38:01.445
then these companies
that want to advertise you to,

00:38:01.487 --> 00:38:04.407
well, advertise their brands,
then that's what they'll do.

00:38:04.407 --> 00:38:05.866
And then, of course,
they're in a situation

00:38:05.908 --> 00:38:07.743
where they can make
their own brand.

00:38:07.785 --> 00:38:10.413
They can have their own brand
and sell that through.

00:38:10.454 --> 00:38:12.206
And then
people will buy it.

00:38:12.248 --> 00:38:14.083
The amount of money
that's poured into the game now

00:38:14.083 --> 00:38:15.751
has risen
their status massively.

00:38:15.751 --> 00:38:20.256
And that also obviously
will incorporate

00:38:20.256 --> 00:38:23.592
that businesses will want
to be linked with them

00:38:23.634 --> 00:38:26.637
and sponsorship deals on top
of that obviously

00:38:26.679 --> 00:38:29.807
helps to increase
their income.

00:38:29.849 --> 00:38:32.435
(narrator)
Following in the footsteps
of a former Man U player,

00:38:32.435 --> 00:38:35.479
Cristiano was on the road
to becoming a legend.

00:38:35.521 --> 00:38:37.189
You know, I've always
liked fashion, you know.

00:38:37.231 --> 00:38:39.942
It's something that,
I like to look nice,

00:38:39.942 --> 00:38:42.320
whether it be on the pitch
or whether it's, uh,

00:38:42.361 --> 00:38:44.488
you know, out
having dinner with family.

00:38:44.530 --> 00:38:46.949
(narrator)
Complete with a high-profile
girlfriend to match.

00:38:46.949 --> 00:38:48.576
Irina Shayk.

00:38:48.617 --> 00:38:50.161
When you're earning
the amounts of money

00:38:50.202 --> 00:38:52.955
these guys are earning now,
especially Cristiano,

00:38:52.955 --> 00:38:57.209
then what else does he probably
got to spend his money on?

00:38:57.251 --> 00:38:58.627
(narrator)
The supermodel and Cristiano

00:38:58.627 --> 00:39:00.296
have been
an item since 2010.

00:39:00.338 --> 00:39:03.257
Another soccer icon,
Lionel Messi,

00:39:03.299 --> 00:39:06.093
faces the similar
daunting task

00:39:06.135 --> 00:39:08.971
of performing on the grand stage
of the World Cup.

00:39:08.971 --> 00:39:11.515
FC Barcelona's Messi
is shorter

00:39:11.557 --> 00:39:15.311
and without the marketable
good looks of Cristiano Ronaldo.

00:39:15.311 --> 00:39:16.645
I just think
the way he plays the game

00:39:16.645 --> 00:39:18.689
and the goals
he scores

00:39:18.731 --> 00:39:22.234
and he just looks,

00:39:22.276 --> 00:39:23.861
you know, spectacular.

00:39:23.903 --> 00:39:25.863
A lot of kids,
probably because

00:39:25.905 --> 00:39:27.823
of his physical
appearance as well,

00:39:27.823 --> 00:39:29.825
would want to be Ronaldo
more than Messi.

00:39:29.825 --> 00:39:33.704
Messi is a great player.
Everyone talks about
the Messi-Ronaldo.

00:39:33.746 --> 00:39:35.790
Messi is a fantastic player,

00:39:35.831 --> 00:39:38.709
but he's a great player in
a very good team, and I think

00:39:38.751 --> 00:39:42.505
Ronaldo's an exceptional
player in a not so good side.

00:39:42.505 --> 00:39:44.924
(narrator)
Ronaldo looks like

00:39:44.965 --> 00:39:47.301
he was constructed
in a footballer factory

00:39:47.343 --> 00:39:50.179
while Messi
is the everyman's player,

00:39:50.179 --> 00:39:52.390
which is why many fans
gravitate to him.

00:39:52.431 --> 00:39:53.849
These two often finish
one and two in most

00:39:53.849 --> 00:39:56.519
of the Player
of the Year Awards,

00:39:56.519 --> 00:39:58.646
and are constantly compared
with one another.

00:39:58.687 --> 00:40:00.815
With Messi being
the build that he is,

00:40:00.856 --> 00:40:03.734
he relies purely and simply
on his footballing ability.

00:40:03.776 --> 00:40:06.862
And for that reason,
I give it to Messi.

00:40:06.862 --> 00:40:09.990
I think you've got your obvious
Messis and your Ronaldos,

00:40:10.032 --> 00:40:13.035
but what I quite want to see is
someone, not necessarily random,

00:40:13.035 --> 00:40:15.371
but coming up
through the ranks

00:40:15.413 --> 00:40:19.208
and maybe a Gonzalo Higuain
from Argentina.

00:40:19.250 --> 00:40:22.169
You know, a star
player, but someone
who isn't necessarily

00:40:22.211 --> 00:40:24.004
as well known as he
probably should be.

00:40:24.046 --> 00:40:26.799
(narrator)
Ronaldo's transfer
to Real Madrid

00:40:26.841 --> 00:40:29.051
only acerbated
the comparisons.

00:40:29.051 --> 00:40:31.220
Messi would take home
the FIFA Ballon d'Or

00:40:31.262 --> 00:40:32.763
for three straight years

00:40:32.805 --> 00:40:35.808
before Ronaldo broke
his streak in 2013.

00:40:35.850 --> 00:40:38.978
(cheering and applause)

00:40:47.653 --> 00:40:50.698
(chattering)

00:41:26.942 --> 00:41:29.236
(female translator)
Good evening.

00:41:29.278 --> 00:41:31.947
There are no words
to describe this moment.

00:41:31.989 --> 00:41:36.452
(cheering)

00:41:44.502 --> 00:41:48.297
I want to thank
all my colleagues

00:41:48.297 --> 00:41:50.799
and companions
at Real Madrid.

00:41:50.841 --> 00:41:53.802
The Brazilian
and the Portuguese team,

00:41:53.802 --> 00:41:55.804
and my family, who is here
with me today.

00:41:55.804 --> 00:41:58.140
(translator)
It's a very important
prize and, like I said

00:41:58.140 --> 00:42:01.143
in the press conference before,
I'm very happy to be amongst

00:42:01.143 --> 00:42:02.645
the three best players.

00:42:02.645 --> 00:42:05.314
For me it's a prize,
like I said,

00:42:05.356 --> 00:42:08.817
Cristiano won it,
and he deserved to win.

00:42:08.817 --> 00:42:12.696
(speaking foreign language)

00:42:26.377 --> 00:42:28.087
(narrator)
Messi and Ronaldo

00:42:28.128 --> 00:42:30.172
may be highly regarded
in the world of football,

00:42:30.172 --> 00:42:33.551
yet on the international stage,
both come up short

00:42:33.592 --> 00:42:37.179
in comparison
to the all-time greats.

00:42:37.179 --> 00:42:41.392
Pelé won three World Cups,
the only player to do so.

00:42:41.433 --> 00:42:43.852
Pelé is the, in my opinion,
the best player I've ever seen,

00:42:43.894 --> 00:42:45.187
and I've got no reason
to change that.

00:42:45.187 --> 00:42:47.523
So I put Pelé
in front of Ronaldo,

00:42:47.523 --> 00:42:49.858
but Ronaldo in front
of Beckham, as players.

00:42:49.900 --> 00:42:52.027
Looks-wise, I'd put
that reverse.

00:42:52.027 --> 00:42:54.613
Beckham, Ronaldo, Pelé,
in the oil painting.

00:42:54.655 --> 00:42:56.407
(narrator)
The other Ronaldo,

00:42:56.448 --> 00:42:59.660
Ronaldo Luis Nazario de Lima,

00:42:59.702 --> 00:43:01.912
won two World Cups
and is the leading

00:43:01.954 --> 00:43:05.374
World Cup goal scorer
with an astonishing 15.

00:43:05.416 --> 00:43:08.544
Diego Maradona
captained Argentina

00:43:08.544 --> 00:43:11.547
to a World Cup victory
in 1986,

00:43:11.589 --> 00:43:13.841
and Sir Bobby Charlton
became a legend

00:43:13.882 --> 00:43:17.052
for helping England
to victory in 1966.

00:43:17.094 --> 00:43:19.346
Bobby's one of the reasons

00:43:19.388 --> 00:43:22.891
that I existed
as long as I did

00:43:22.891 --> 00:43:24.226
in the early days
at Manchester United

00:43:24.226 --> 00:43:25.936
because he believed in me.

00:43:25.978 --> 00:43:28.105
He believed in the route,
the direction

00:43:28.147 --> 00:43:30.065
that Manchester had taken

00:43:30.065 --> 00:43:32.901
in terms of producing
our young players again.

00:43:32.901 --> 00:43:35.904
And Bobby played an integral
part in that,

00:43:35.946 --> 00:43:38.240
and I thank him
today for that.

00:43:38.240 --> 00:43:40.326
(narrator)
This is the international stage

00:43:40.367 --> 00:43:43.746
where football's elite
become legends.

00:43:43.787 --> 00:43:46.582
With an audience
of over 700 million people

00:43:46.582 --> 00:43:48.792
watching from all corners
of the globe,

00:43:48.834 --> 00:43:50.544
it's on this stage
that the stars

00:43:50.586 --> 00:43:52.463
of the game really shine.

00:43:52.504 --> 00:43:55.132
World Cup defeats
have placed a lot of pressure

00:43:55.174 --> 00:43:57.092
on this summer's
2014 campaign

00:43:57.134 --> 00:43:58.636
for Ronaldo and Messi alike.

00:43:58.677 --> 00:44:01.555
(translator)
Well, when the draw happened,

00:44:01.597 --> 00:44:02.598
I was not watching.

00:44:02.598 --> 00:44:04.850
I was actually sleeping.

00:44:04.892 --> 00:44:07.144
I think I have to be
honest with you.

00:44:07.186 --> 00:44:09.271
It's an extremely
difficult group with Germany,

00:44:09.271 --> 00:44:11.774
who are always one of
the favorites for the title,

00:44:11.774 --> 00:44:14.276
and the others,
the United States and Ghana,

00:44:14.276 --> 00:44:16.236
who also have great teams.

00:44:16.278 --> 00:44:19.239
That's why I think
it is a difficult group.

00:44:19.281 --> 00:44:20.949
Portugal came
through the playoffs

00:44:20.991 --> 00:44:23.285
after the qualification
for the World Cup,

00:44:23.285 --> 00:44:25.120
so there's a good chance
that they could be

00:44:25.162 --> 00:44:26.872
the dark horses
of the World Cup.

00:44:26.914 --> 00:44:28.916
I think in that group,

00:44:28.957 --> 00:44:33.671
Russia will be
more constant than has.

00:44:33.712 --> 00:44:38.342
They play better,
and, um, we drop.

00:44:41.512 --> 00:44:44.014
Not in a few
moments, points,

00:44:44.056 --> 00:44:46.975
that you should don't--
don't lost.

00:44:46.975 --> 00:44:49.687
But it's the past,
so we play the playoffs,

00:44:49.728 --> 00:44:51.522
it was good for us.

00:44:51.563 --> 00:44:54.692
We win both games,
we play very, very good.

00:44:54.733 --> 00:44:56.652
(narrator)
But for Messi and Ronaldo

00:44:56.652 --> 00:45:00.322
to establish themselves as two
of the game's all-time bests,

00:45:00.322 --> 00:45:02.116
they will have to win.

00:45:02.157 --> 00:45:04.827
Important-- all competitions
is important,

00:45:04.868 --> 00:45:09.665
and this one is a special
one because it was in Brazil,

00:45:09.665 --> 00:45:12.000
will be in Brazil.

00:45:12.042 --> 00:45:15.087
For us, Portuguese country,
it's very important

00:45:15.129 --> 00:45:18.716
because you know, we--
we have history with Brazil,

00:45:18.757 --> 00:45:21.343
the culture, and...

00:45:21.343 --> 00:45:25.180
And we speak
the same language.
So it's fantastic.

00:45:25.180 --> 00:45:29.852
We are so proud
to be part of this big event.

00:45:29.852 --> 00:45:32.563
I think Cristiano's chances
of becoming a legend

00:45:32.604 --> 00:45:34.356
this World Cup
will unfortunately

00:45:34.356 --> 00:45:38.652
not be solely determined
by him and him alone.

00:45:38.694 --> 00:45:42.740
It will depend on how
the team as a whole performs.

00:45:42.781 --> 00:45:44.366
If he can do that again,

00:45:44.366 --> 00:45:49.371
then he will earn
that legend status.

00:45:49.371 --> 00:45:53.000
And rightly so, if he could take
Portugal through to win
the World Cup.

00:45:53.041 --> 00:45:54.877
Portuguese is
the same language,

00:45:54.918 --> 00:45:57.671
we have a lot
of Portuguese there,

00:45:57.713 --> 00:46:00.549
and we are very happy
for that.

00:46:00.549 --> 00:46:03.385
And we, we try
to enjoy the,

00:46:03.385 --> 00:46:05.220
you know, World Cup,
it's, uh,

00:46:05.262 --> 00:46:07.264
the main competition
for national teams

00:46:07.306 --> 00:46:09.057
so we try to enjoy.

00:46:12.561 --> 00:46:13.896
(narrator)
In addition to any pressure

00:46:13.896 --> 00:46:15.731
placed on the players,
the host country

00:46:15.731 --> 00:46:17.733
had its own set
of issues to sort through.

00:46:17.775 --> 00:46:20.527
Though Brazil was excited
about hosting the World Cup,

00:46:20.569 --> 00:46:23.280
the cost of the event,
with the massive security

00:46:23.322 --> 00:46:25.908
to not only protect the players
but the fans as well,

00:46:25.908 --> 00:46:29.870
the stadium construction
costs well over $3 billion.

00:46:29.912 --> 00:46:32.247
Regardless, countries
heavily vied for the chance

00:46:32.247 --> 00:46:34.124
of becoming the host country.

00:46:34.166 --> 00:46:36.418
England sent its own football
legend and a future king

00:46:36.418 --> 00:46:39.296
to seal the deal,
but to no avail.

00:46:39.338 --> 00:46:42.800
Even after winning the bid,
but years before
the actual event,

00:46:42.841 --> 00:46:46.804
problems arise,
as in the case of Qatar.

00:46:46.845 --> 00:46:50.682
However, with Pelé as the face
of Brazil's World Cup event,

00:46:50.724 --> 00:46:53.977
this one is sure to become
an event for the record books.

00:46:54.019 --> 00:46:55.938
(Pelé)
Was a surprise to everyone

00:46:55.938 --> 00:46:58.148
what happened Brazil

00:46:58.190 --> 00:47:00.108
because, uh,

00:47:00.108 --> 00:47:01.985
this is
a political problem,

00:47:02.027 --> 00:47:05.948
'cause I mention
about the--

00:47:05.989 --> 00:47:10.118
the football
is the big promotion

00:47:10.160 --> 00:47:12.162
of Brazilian country.

00:47:12.204 --> 00:47:15.415
Then when you have
an event

00:47:15.457 --> 00:47:19.711
like, uh, World Cup,

00:47:19.753 --> 00:47:21.797
like Confederation Cup,

00:47:21.797 --> 00:47:25.843
uh, you have Olympics,
you know,

00:47:25.884 --> 00:47:28.303
then I think everybody
should be together.

00:47:28.303 --> 00:47:30.722
But this is
a political problem.

00:47:30.764 --> 00:47:33.684
We have that,
but no doubt, no doubt,

00:47:33.725 --> 00:47:37.354
the World Cup
will be fantastic.

00:47:37.396 --> 00:47:39.982
(narrator)
Love him or hate him,
you can't deny

00:47:39.982 --> 00:47:42.818
that Ronaldo's impact
on the sport is immense.

00:47:42.860 --> 00:47:44.319
He moves the needle.

00:47:44.319 --> 00:47:45.821
Whether you're cheering
his every goal

00:47:45.863 --> 00:47:49.324
or cursing his name,
he triggers a reaction.

00:47:49.366 --> 00:47:51.827
He's one of the faces
of the game.

00:47:51.869 --> 00:47:54.663
And that face will once again
be placed under the microscope

00:47:54.705 --> 00:47:57.332
in Brazil, where the game's
best and brightest

00:47:57.332 --> 00:48:01.378
will compete in front
of 700 million viewers.

00:48:01.420 --> 00:48:04.256
In the World Cup,
questions are answered,

00:48:04.298 --> 00:48:07.384
and the pressure to perform
is nothing short of daunting.

00:48:07.426 --> 00:48:09.636
Once you reach
a World Cup, this...

00:48:09.678 --> 00:48:11.054
you know, anything
can happen.

00:48:20.439 --> 00:48:23.358
(narrator)
To play at the World Cup
is an honor,

00:48:23.358 --> 00:48:26.528
and one that players
take incredibly seriously.

00:48:26.528 --> 00:48:28.614
The pressure of playing for
your country is much greater

00:48:28.655 --> 00:48:31.950
than playing for your club
for the simple reason

00:48:31.992 --> 00:48:34.077
that you've got--
you're not only pleasing

00:48:34.119 --> 00:48:35.996
one set of supporters,
you're trying to please

00:48:36.038 --> 00:48:39.374
the whole, um, obviously,
the whole country.

00:48:39.416 --> 00:48:42.544
And that, hence,
there's pressure with that

00:48:42.544 --> 00:48:45.047
in that respect, and you've
also got the pressure

00:48:45.047 --> 00:48:49.718
of trying to make people
understand and believe
that you should be there,

00:48:49.718 --> 00:48:52.554
possibly in front
of their own favorite player
that plays for their club.

00:48:52.554 --> 00:48:53.555
(screaming)

00:48:53.555 --> 00:48:57.517
(chanting)

00:48:57.559 --> 00:48:58.936
We deserve to win 100%.

00:49:07.277 --> 00:49:09.571
Fast forward a couple of months
and we find Ronaldo

00:49:09.571 --> 00:49:12.574
on the practice pitch
with his Real Madrid teammates.

00:49:12.574 --> 00:49:17.162
His performance at the 2014
World Cup is now a distant
memory.

00:49:17.204 --> 00:49:20.040
Fresh from winning
the UEFA Champions League Cup,

00:49:20.082 --> 00:49:22.167
there were high hopes
for the Portuguese striker

00:49:22.209 --> 00:49:25.963
as he scored 17 goals
in that tournament.

00:49:26.004 --> 00:49:27.923
And that's not counting
the assists.

00:49:27.965 --> 00:49:32.678
Well, it was an unbelievable
night to win "La Decima"
here in Portugal

00:49:32.719 --> 00:49:35.847
with all this beautiful crowd

00:49:35.889 --> 00:49:39.226
and it's something
that we're looking many,
many years of.

00:49:39.267 --> 00:49:42.354
(man)
Cristiano Ronaldo does it again.

00:49:42.396 --> 00:49:45.732
Every year,
I tried to do my best.
I score goals,

00:49:45.774 --> 00:49:47.943
and I help the team.

00:49:47.985 --> 00:49:49.903
(narrator)
He also took a lot
of punishment,

00:49:49.945 --> 00:49:51.780
irritating a chronic injury.

00:49:51.822 --> 00:49:54.992
An injury that would
follow him to Brazil.

00:49:55.033 --> 00:49:59.287
Ronaldo's arrival was coupled
with both excitement
and speculation.

00:50:02.624 --> 00:50:04.543
He was in great spirits
upon arriving.

00:50:11.133 --> 00:50:16.138
But it was a different story
during practice sessions
in full view of the press.

00:50:16.138 --> 00:50:18.306
We wanna win.
We can win.

00:50:18.306 --> 00:50:22.185
We know it's gonna be difficult,
but I think we are
in good shape.

00:50:22.227 --> 00:50:24.646
(narrator)
He played brilliantly during
team qualifiers,

00:50:24.646 --> 00:50:28.316
but it was not the same
Ronaldo who took the pitch
against Germany

00:50:28.316 --> 00:50:30.235
in Portugal's opening match.

00:50:32.154 --> 00:50:35.032
And the look on Ronaldo's
face said it all.

00:50:36.908 --> 00:50:40.245
With a 4-0 defeat
and a red card for Pepe,

00:50:40.287 --> 00:50:43.790
Portugal's hopes for victory
were all but gone.

00:50:43.832 --> 00:50:47.002
Obviously, it was

00:50:47.044 --> 00:50:49.546
a difficult situation
to accept.

00:50:49.588 --> 00:50:54.301
But there is body language
that many, many times

00:50:54.342 --> 00:50:58.847
pushed the referees
to have these kind of decisions

00:50:58.847 --> 00:51:02.684
and to leave a team playing
with ten men

00:51:02.684 --> 00:51:04.352
for such a long time

00:51:04.352 --> 00:51:09.274
is obviously a big handicap
for the team.

00:51:09.316 --> 00:51:11.193
(narrator)
Ronaldo may have had
the game-changing assist

00:51:11.234 --> 00:51:13.695
in the game against the USA.

00:51:13.695 --> 00:51:16.823
(man)
Here's Cristiano Ronaldo,
oh it's a great cross!

00:51:16.865 --> 00:51:18.033
and it is an equalizer!

00:51:18.075 --> 00:51:20.160
(narrator)
But it was too late to change
the outcome.

00:51:20.202 --> 00:51:22.370
USA and Germany would advance

00:51:22.412 --> 00:51:25.415
and Ronaldo would
return back to Europe.

00:51:25.457 --> 00:51:28.502
Now back with Real Madrid
and in better shape,

00:51:28.543 --> 00:51:30.504
the old Ronaldo has truly
returned

00:51:30.545 --> 00:51:33.924
as he scored both goals
in a UEFA game against Seville.

00:51:33.965 --> 00:51:37.886
(man)
Gets it on to Benzema,
on it goes to Ronaldo.

00:51:37.886 --> 00:51:39.054
Oh, yeah!

00:51:39.096 --> 00:51:42.432
It was amazing.
A fantastic evening.

00:51:42.474 --> 00:51:45.435
We win a very important trophy,

00:51:45.477 --> 00:51:49.731
and I didn't play fantastic.

00:51:49.731 --> 00:51:52.859
I scored two goals,
which in my opinion,

00:51:52.901 --> 00:51:55.362
it was very important
for me to give me confidence

00:51:55.403 --> 00:51:57.823
to start well the season.

00:51:57.864 --> 00:52:00.742
So I'm good, I feel happy,
one trophy.

00:52:00.742 --> 00:52:02.577
So very good.

00:52:02.577 --> 00:52:05.080
(narrator)
However, even with this
promising outcome,

00:52:05.080 --> 00:52:07.999
his injury came back
to haunt him.

00:52:08.041 --> 00:52:12.003
Many say it's time for this
legendary footballer
to take a break.

00:52:12.045 --> 00:52:15.423
If the injury persists,
Ronaldo's career in football

00:52:15.423 --> 00:52:17.342
could come to an untimely end.

00:52:19.719 --> 00:52:23.640
And there are other teams
that have Ronaldo
in their sights.

00:52:23.682 --> 00:52:27.352
As Beckham builds momentum
for football in the US.

00:52:27.394 --> 00:52:34.151
We don't want public funding. We
will fund the stadium ourselves,

00:52:34.192 --> 00:52:36.278
create a stadium.
We wanna create a soccer team,
a football club

00:52:36.319 --> 00:52:38.071
that is the people's
football club.

00:52:38.113 --> 00:52:40.448
It's simple as that.
You know, I've worked

00:52:40.490 --> 00:52:42.617
for some of the biggest clubs
in the world

00:52:42.617 --> 00:52:45.537
with some of the greatest
players in the world,

00:52:45.579 --> 00:52:47.622
and this is a dream.

00:52:47.622 --> 00:52:50.125
If someone would have turned
around to me at 11 years old

00:52:50.125 --> 00:52:54.129
and said, "You're gonna play
for Manchester United.

00:52:54.171 --> 00:52:56.464
You're gonna represent England.
You're gonna play
for Real Madrid,

00:52:56.506 --> 00:52:58.967
AC Milan, the Galaxy

00:52:59.009 --> 00:53:02.804
and then become an owner,"
I probably wouldn't have
believed them.

00:53:02.804 --> 00:53:04.431
(narrator)
Don't be surprised

00:53:04.472 --> 00:53:06.474
if Ronaldo decides
to cross the Atlantic too.

00:53:06.474 --> 00:53:10.187
- The girls love you.
- No, love you because maybe
I play good football.

00:53:10.228 --> 00:53:12.480
Yeah, what about Galaxy?
Are you gonna join the Galaxy?

00:53:12.522 --> 00:53:14.482
Yeah, you know,

00:53:14.482 --> 00:53:16.943
- Beckham and Abel Xavier
played there.
- Yeah.

00:53:16.985 --> 00:53:19.821
And I spoke with
him a few times.
He says it's great.

00:53:19.821 --> 00:53:22.115
You should play here,
maybe in the future.
You never know.

00:53:22.157 --> 00:53:25.827
He's such a talent.
He's such a great player
and a good person.

00:53:25.827 --> 00:53:29.497
You know, he's one of the best
if not the best player
in the world.

00:53:29.539 --> 00:53:33.335
So watching him is

00:53:33.335 --> 00:53:35.837
a huge pleasure
for many Real Madrid fans.

00:53:35.837 --> 00:53:37.505
(narrator)
Believe it or not,
this footballer may also have

00:53:37.547 --> 00:53:40.008
his sights set
on a different sort of stage.

00:53:40.050 --> 00:53:43.178
The silver screens of Hollywood.

00:53:43.178 --> 00:53:45.347
(shouting)

00:53:50.227 --> 00:53:53.188
And he always has time
for charity.

00:53:53.230 --> 00:53:55.357
Proving that even
a freezing shower of ice

00:53:55.357 --> 00:53:57.108
isn't enough to make him flinch.

00:53:57.150 --> 00:53:59.778
Ronaldo accepted
the Ice Bucket Challenge

00:53:59.819 --> 00:54:02.405
and lent his support
to the ALS Association

00:54:02.447 --> 00:54:04.699
in order to raise money
for this worthy cause.

00:54:04.741 --> 00:54:07.452
- (screams)
- (laughing)

00:54:07.494 --> 00:54:09.371
Following in the footsteps
of some of the world's
biggest names,

00:54:09.412 --> 00:54:12.249
ranging from director
Steven Spielberg.

00:54:12.290 --> 00:54:15.001
Oh, man!

00:54:15.043 --> 00:54:16.211
(narrator)
To David Beckham.

00:54:16.211 --> 00:54:18.296
(laughing)

00:54:18.338 --> 00:54:20.882
(narrator)
Even top fashion editor,
Anna Wintour of "Vogue."

00:54:20.882 --> 00:54:23.051
(shrieking)

00:54:23.093 --> 00:54:27.222
The idea is to have a freezing
bucket of ice water poured
on your head,

00:54:27.264 --> 00:54:30.850
and bring attention
to a very worthy cause.

00:54:30.892 --> 00:54:34.354
In America, the disease is known
as Lou Gehrig's Disease.

00:54:34.396 --> 00:54:37.232
and in the UK
as motor neuron disease,

00:54:37.274 --> 00:54:39.734
but the symptoms and effects
are the same

00:54:39.734 --> 00:54:43.405
and devastating to sufferers
and their families.

00:54:43.405 --> 00:54:46.616
- For the past two weeks...
- For the past two weeks...

00:54:46.658 --> 00:54:50.287
- For the past two weeks...
- You have been reading
about the bad break I got.

00:54:50.328 --> 00:54:54.416
- Yet today...
- Yet today I consider myself...

00:54:54.416 --> 00:54:57.544
- I consider myself...
- I consider myself...

00:54:57.585 --> 00:54:59.462
the luckiest man

00:54:59.504 --> 00:55:03.300
on the face of the Earth.

00:55:03.341 --> 00:55:06.803
(narrator)
It's of great importance
that people like Ronaldo

00:55:06.845 --> 00:55:09.848
bring such a high volume
of attention to this disease.

00:55:09.889 --> 00:55:12.517
As it is thought with the right
funding and the right direction,

00:55:12.559 --> 00:55:14.477
this disease could be beaten.

00:55:16.354 --> 00:55:18.440
Regardless of what
the future holds,

00:55:18.440 --> 00:55:21.151
Ronaldo had made his mark
in history.

00:55:21.192 --> 00:55:23.611
One of the best
if not the best player
in the world.

00:55:23.653 --> 00:55:26.031
So for me it was
a fantastic year

00:55:26.072 --> 00:55:28.491
and I win all
the individual awards.

00:55:28.533 --> 00:55:31.077
(shouting)

00:55:31.119 --> 00:55:33.455
(cheering)

00:55:33.455 --> 00:55:37.167
This trophy is
for collective awards.
I'm really, really happy.

00:55:37.208 --> 00:55:40.462
(narrator)
Whether it's a football pitch,
red carpet or magazine cover,

00:55:40.503 --> 00:55:44.632
one thing is certain--
Ronaldo is here to stay

00:55:44.632 --> 00:55:47.427
and he certainly has
the world at his feet.

